# Anchoring note. Every pattern below that is a bare
# name — no internal slash — matches at ANY depth, not just at the
# repository root. This tree commits an `examples/` holding a Kiln project
# tree and a corpus, so a directory named `lib`, `build`, `var`, `target`,
# `instance`, `env` or `cover` inside it would be untracked in silence. The
# build- and tool-artifact patterns are therefore anchored with a leading `/`. Caches (`__pycache__/`,
# `.pytest_cache/`, `.ruff_cache/`, `.mypy_cache/`, `*.egg-info/`, `.venv`)
# stay unanchored on purpose: they are produced next to whatever they
# describe and never hold content. `*.log` also stays unanchored: a run
# writes its log in the state folder, not here, and the examples commit no
# `.log` fixture.

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
/.Python
/build/
/develop-eggs/
/dist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/
/share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
/.installed.cfg
*.egg
/MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#   Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#   before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
/*.manifest
/*.spec

# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

