.pypirc

# Marimo
/marimo/_static/
/marimo/_lsp/
/__marimo__/

# Streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Old run outputs. A run keeps its state in the state folder
# (`~/.kiln_ai/harness_tuner/`, or `$KILN_HARNESS_TUNER_HOME`), never in this
# tree. A checkout used before that move still holds its `runs/` (run
# scratch), `traces/` (the session transcripts the dispatcher copied out) and
# `reports/`. They are a user's local output, not committed evidence, and
# nothing moves them: delete them or move them out. Root-anchored, because a
# Kiln project tree under `examples/` carries its own `tasks/<id>/runs/` — see
# the note at the end of this file.
/runs/
/traces/
/reports/
# Local Kiln projects you point the loop at. Never tracked. One Kiln project
# per subfolder.
/targets/

# A Kiln project under `examples/` is committed without its runs. Kiln writes
# them when a project is used in place rather than copied out: the task's runs
# at `tasks/<id>/runs/` and each eval config's EvalRuns at
# `tasks/<id>/evals/<id>/configs/<id>/runs/`. Their ids come from the server,
# outside the invented `424242……` band, and a model run is sampled, so a run
# is not reproducible. What is committed is the corpus that produces them.
/examples/*/*/tasks/**/runs/

# Installed by `harness-tuner-install-agents --dest .` from
# `src/kiln_harness_tuner/agent_files/`: the skills in each agent CLI's own
# layout, and Claude Code's `kiln_api_mcp` server. `agent_files/` is the
# source. The root `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are the tracked contributor
# guide, not install targets.
/.agents/
/.claude/skills/
/.claude/settings.json
/.mcp.json

# Spec-driven development: per-user state and local review artifacts.
/.specs_skill_state/
/reviews/
